WEBVTT

00:00:01.820 --> 00:00:03.970
I can see it. I can see it!

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:06.640
A new encounter for the master.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.470
I can sure see it!

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:10.650
A new encounter?

00:00:10.650 --> 00:00:12.870
The goddesses of fate, 
ladies and gentlemen...

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:17.810
They've told the master about 
his luck for the new semester!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.830
I don't care about my luck,

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.820
but you insisted.

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:23.940
Now, now...

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.980
So what is this new encounter?

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:31.960
And why do we have to 
wear these heavy things?

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:34.170
We're supposed to be goddesses.

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:40.010
Don't say that. Cait Sith said 
these are the latest in fashion!

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:43.370
His ideas about trends are all messed up!

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:45.640
I don't want to dress like that!

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:47.750
The new semester starts tomorrow, chirp?

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.850
What a way to start it, huh, chirp?

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.970
Good luck, Yushi, chirp!

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:53.200
Thanks...

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:54.530
Chirpity-chirp! Chirp!

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:30.370
<b>Fifteenth Haunting 
A New Teacher Arrives</b>

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:32.580
Now, I'll introduce the teacher who will 
replace Hayasaka-sensei while he's ill.

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:34.750
Naomi Chiaki-sensei.

00:02:36.170 --> 00:02:37.330
<i>Chiaki?</i>

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:39.500
<i>Naomi? A woman?</i>

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:45.180
He will be teaching accounting and computers.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:48.630
He will also oversee homeroom for Class 2-C.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:54.580
I-It's a man...

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.060
Lucky me!

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.500
<i>But he doesn't seem like a teacher...</i>

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:05.990
And I will also introduce Miura-sensei's 
replacement, as well.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:09.610
Haruka Aoki-sensei.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:11.960
She'll be in charge of Class 2-A.

00:03:20.890 --> 00:03:22.990
I am Kamiya, the student council president.

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.970
On behalf of all the students,

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.210
I welcome you,

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:29.670
Chiaki-sensei, Aoki-sensei.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.610
Nice to meet you.

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:33.070
Nice to meet you.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:39.290
Chiaki-chan's so cool!

00:03:39.290 --> 00:03:40.990
He's starting today, right?

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.100
Aoki was hot, huh?

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.400
Maybe I'll study extra hard in English!

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:52.320
Okay, we're starting homeroom!

00:03:55.740 --> 00:04:00.550
The principal introduced me, but I'm 
the homeroom teacher for 2-C.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:04.430
<b>Naomi Chiaki</b>

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.370
The name's Naomi Chiaki.

00:04:02.370 --> 00:04:03.320
Nice to meet you.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:11.680
His body's so nice...

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.030
Question, Sensei!

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:14.840
What?

00:04:14.840 --> 00:04:16.770
Are you single—

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.640
Hey!

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:20.230
I'm 32, and I'm single.

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:30.580
<b>Naomi Chiaki</b>

00:04:20.230 --> 00:04:21.860
My family is rich.

00:04:22.830 --> 00:04:27.710
But if you want to do anything 
with me, graduate first.

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:29.760
Once you graduate, it'll be fine.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:33.200
<i>He's easy to get along with.</i>

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:35.570
Where do you live, Sensei?

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:37.000
East Takanodai.

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:39.180
Do you play a sport?

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:41.840
I've done aikido since I was a kid.

00:04:41.840 --> 00:04:45.270
Does the rest of your family teach?

00:04:45.460 --> 00:04:48.430
My cousin is a teacher at 
a girls' middle school.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:51.220
What's your favorite type of girl?

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.480
Girls, huh?

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:58.510
Sexy ones with big boobs...

00:04:54.480 --> 00:05:00.020
<b>Naomi Chiaki</b>

00:05:01.060 --> 00:05:03.290
<i>What kind of questions are these?</i>

00:05:03.570 --> 00:05:06.640
Well, since I'm replacing Hayasaka-sensei,

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.480
I'll also be in charge of 
guidance counseling.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:13.250
But I'm still new at this.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:16.160
I haven't been teaching for even a decade.

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:18.210
And due to that, I'm young,

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.430
which means I know how you guys feel.

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.510
I understand that this stuff 
is interesting, but...

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:29.130
Ow.

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.010
This is confiscated!

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:35.240
<i>So that's all the punishment he gets?</i>

00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:39.230
<i>I thought he reminded me of someone...</i>

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:40.430
<i>It's Akira-san.</i>

00:05:40.710 --> 00:05:44.110
<i>Popular, rough, and gutsy.</i>

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:46.790
All right, we're changing seats.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:48.280
We'll draw straws, okay?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:53.520
Hello, members of Class 2-C.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.970
I am Haruka Aoki.

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:58.550
Since the school year is underway, 
I realize there will be some confusion.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:06:00.870
But let's work hard at our studies!

00:06:02.190 --> 00:06:05.630
"To be or not to be, that is the question.

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:09.180
Whether 'tis nobler in the mind to suffer

00:06:09.180 --> 00:06:12.290
the slings and arrows of outrageous fortune,

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:15.280
or to take arms against a sea of troubles,

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:20.230
and by opposing end them. 
To die, to sleep no more.

00:06:16.330 --> 00:06:18.150
<i>Hmm, she's easy to understand.</i>

00:06:18.780 --> 00:06:21.220
<i>She seems really prim and proper,</i>

00:06:20.230 --> 00:06:22.370
<i>And by a sleep, to say we end."</i>

00:06:21.220 --> 00:06:22.370
<i>unlike Chiaki.</i>

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:27.170
All right, are there any questions so far?

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:31.830
She was even prettier up close.

00:06:31.830 --> 00:06:34.940
Yeah, so slender! I wish I looked like her!

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:39.510
Aoki-sensei is great, 
but Chiaki-sensei's better! He's so awesome!

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:41.260
Right? He's so cool!

00:06:41.260 --> 00:06:44.650
Yeah, he's really cool.
And he's fun when he talks.

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.570
Right? Right?

00:06:45.570 --> 00:06:47.390
I wish he'd talk more.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:50.170
I'm sure he has lots of funny stories!

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.780
Well, I don't have a bad 
opinion of him, either.

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:54.340
You get it, Inaba!

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.240
But I think I know why Chiaki-sensei 
is doing guidance counseling.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:01.690
It feels like he'd help you with 
even the weirdest problems!

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.770
What do you mean by weird problems?

00:07:04.070 --> 00:07:07.310
But couldn't you talk to Aoki-sensei 
about your problems, too?

00:07:07.310 --> 00:07:08.690
She seems nice.

00:07:09.340 --> 00:07:11.370
I don't know...

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:14.130
You couldn't say anything weird to her.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.520
When you say "weird," what do you mean?

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:19.360
You know! Weird stuff!

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:24.920
Inaba, you couldn't go to her 
with pervy problems, could you?

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:27.500
I wouldn't do that! 
And don't drag me into this!

00:07:27.500 --> 00:07:28.740
What's this?

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:31.670
What kind of pervy problems 
does Inaba-kun have?

00:07:31.670 --> 00:07:32.770
Don't ask me!

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:40.380
<i>Well, I definitely couldn't go to 
her with anything like that...</i>

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:43.400
<i>She's got this kind of air about her 
that wouldn't allow it, you know?</i>

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:47.910
<i>And you need to be careful who you 
discuss your problems with, too.</i>

00:07:48.150 --> 00:07:50.570
<i>People can be good at some 
things and bad at others.</i>

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:52.620
Indeed!

00:07:52.850 --> 00:07:55.780
Two new teachers...

00:07:55.780 --> 00:07:58.660
The Norns' fortunetelling was correct!

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:01.940
Yeah. So amazing.

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:04.800
But I'm glad both were good teachers.

00:08:04.800 --> 00:08:06.130
Indeed...

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:10.710
The woman's aura was especially pure!

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:12.670
Oh? That's rare.

00:08:12.670 --> 00:08:17.050
You always say human auras are tainted, 
so you don't want to sense them.

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:19.750
Normally, yes!

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:26.270
Human auras are always wavering, 
warped by various desires and emotions.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:33.080
But those who have undergone spiritual 
training lack that fluctuation!

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:37.610
Like that black mage you admire.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:38.980
Ryu-san?

00:08:38.980 --> 00:08:41.930
A person of strong beliefs, you could say.

00:08:41.930 --> 00:08:48.650
The aura unique to one who focuses 
each day on mastering his path.

00:08:49.350 --> 00:08:52.540
Then, Aoki-sensei must be 
a very good person, right?

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.300
Not necessarily a good person.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:01.590
It is simply that her aura is pure.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:06.230
<b>Joutou Business High School</b>

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.740
Hey, Inaba.

00:09:07.740 --> 00:09:08.650
You got a second?

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:09.980
Chiaki-sensei?

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:12.660
What? What? Do you need something?

00:09:12.660 --> 00:09:15.400
I heard you live alone in an apartment.

00:09:15.630 --> 00:09:19.030
As your teacher, should I 
visit your home once?

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.630
No, there's no problem...

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:25.580
Naturally. You get good grades and 
seem to take things seriously.

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:27.340
I can neglect you, right?

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:29.560
<i>He's a very direct teacher.</i>

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:31.370
It's okay.

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:34.470
I won't do anything stupid. 
My livelihood is on the line.

00:09:35.190 --> 00:09:36.550
A good answer.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.540
Wh-What?

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.460
All right! Bye.

00:09:46.440 --> 00:09:48.200
<i>What was that?</i>

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.410
It isn't fair that he only talks to you!

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:56.020
What are you talking about? Okay, let's go!

00:09:56.360 --> 00:09:59.710
It isn't fair he only talks to you! Not fair!

00:09:58.100 --> 00:09:59.710
Stop it...

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:01.460
Sorry for being late!

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:05.950
Inaba and Tashiro, perfect timing.

00:10:05.950 --> 00:10:09.110
I was just about to introduce 
a new club member.

00:10:09.110 --> 00:10:10.720
A new club member?

00:10:10.720 --> 00:10:12.040
At this time of year?

00:10:12.040 --> 00:10:14.700
Yes, she joined for the new semester.

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:17.670
Konatsu Yamamoto, class 1-F.

00:10:17.990 --> 00:10:19.800
Everyone, look after her.

00:10:34.480 --> 00:10:42.370
<b>About the upcoming social with
the Foreigners Club</b>

00:10:34.960 --> 00:10:36.350
Today,

00:10:36.350 --> 00:10:42.110
we'll decide what we're doing for the upcoming
social with the Foreigners Club.

00:10:42.110 --> 00:10:43.830
Okay!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:47.160
Last year, we dubbed an 
anime movie into English.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:48.650
What should we do this year?

00:10:48.650 --> 00:10:50.990
Last year's event was pretty popular.

00:10:50.990 --> 00:10:52.040
That's right.

00:10:52.040 --> 00:10:55.460
A lot of children come to it, so an 
anime was the right choice.

00:10:55.460 --> 00:10:58.820
Then, should we do that again this year?

00:10:58.820 --> 00:11:00.320
No objections!

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:07.380
Konatsu-chan!

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:10.000
Konatsu is such a cute name.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:12.180
I'm Tashiro, from 2-C.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:15.230
Is there an anime movie you like?

00:11:17.970 --> 00:11:19.070
English...

00:11:20.310 --> 00:11:23.200
You don't speak English at all, do you?

00:11:23.590 --> 00:11:29.120
In the English Conversation Club, I assumed
 you'd speak English the whole time.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.640
Of course not!

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:35.600
Konatsu-chan, you're so serious!

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:40.760
<b>Country of Cherry Blossoms</b>

00:11:36.500 --> 00:11:40.750
Oh, you like books? What kind 
of book are you reading?

00:11:40.750 --> 00:11:42.290
Chekhov.

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:44.650
Chekhov?

00:11:44.910 --> 00:11:46.880
What does that mean?

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:49.070
It's the name of the author.

00:11:49.070 --> 00:11:50.430
Oh, that's it!

00:11:53.130 --> 00:11:55.990
Russian literature is great, isn't it?

00:11:55.990 --> 00:11:57.770
Dostoevsky is good, too,

00:11:57.770 --> 00:11:59.860
but I like Chekhov.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:03.610
Isn't his depiction of the plight 
facing the fin-de-siècle

00:12:03.610 --> 00:12:05.820
intelligentsia and peasantry moving?

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:08.350
I... I see.

00:12:08.350 --> 00:12:11.380
I only read samurai fiction 
and adventure novels...

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:15.280
I always buy the latest <i>Engine 
World and Military Clothes</i>.

00:12:15.280 --> 00:12:17.360
That isn't a novel!

00:12:17.360 --> 00:12:18.590
What?

00:12:20.490 --> 00:12:22.380
Okay, everyone in your seats!

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:26.260
<b>About the upcoming social with
the Foreigners Club</b>

00:12:22.700 --> 00:12:26.260
Tell me what anime movies you'd like to see.

00:12:27.340 --> 00:12:29.220
I'd like to suggest my favorites,

00:12:29.220 --> 00:12:31.090
but if we want one for kids...

00:12:31.090 --> 00:12:32.760
Why anime?

00:12:34.510 --> 00:12:37.100
Why not a normal movie?

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:38.770
No...

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:40.920
We just decided...

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:42.770
...to go with an anime movie, right?

00:12:42.770 --> 00:12:44.820
You're in high school.

00:12:44.820 --> 00:12:47.130
Shouldn't you be getting over anime?

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:51.950
Anime is for little kids.

00:12:52.860 --> 00:12:56.340
Anime isn't for little kids!

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.390
Tashiro, that isn't what we're discussing.

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:03.460
Then, do you have any 
suggestions, Yamamoto-san?

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:06.310
This may be slightly difficult,

00:13:06.310 --> 00:13:08.880
but perhaps we should choose Truffaut.

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:11.490
Truffle? Like a mushroom?

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:12.640
Have you heard of that?

00:13:12.640 --> 00:13:13.550
No...

00:13:16.200 --> 00:13:17.500
Never mind.

00:13:17.990 --> 00:13:19.580
What's her problem?

00:13:21.400 --> 00:13:23.320
<b>My Neighbor     Dragon     Pocke</b>

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:25.060
That's enough for today.

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:27.410
<b>My Neighbor Todo    Dragon Bat    Pocket Star    Natade</b>

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:27.410
Next time, let's decide our candidates.

00:13:27.410 --> 00:13:28.550
Good work today!

00:13:35.910 --> 00:13:37.830
<b>Truffaut...?</b>

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:41.430
Well, there's a problem child!

00:13:41.430 --> 00:13:43.590
That was a surprise. What was that?

00:13:43.590 --> 00:13:45.960
What do we do with that movie?

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:47.610
To begin with, it isn't in Japanese.

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:50.340
It would be good English practice.

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:55.730
But Truffaut was... a French movie director.

00:14:01.620 --> 00:14:03.860
Russian literature and Truffaut, huh?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.900
Those are for the hardcore.

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:11.530
Yeah... But it doesn't seem right.

00:14:11.530 --> 00:14:13.810
But with the way she talked...

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:15.900
It sounds like a complex.

00:14:15.900 --> 00:14:18.080
That's it! You think so?

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:24.710
Fifteen, reading Russian 
literature? Yeah, right!

00:14:24.710 --> 00:14:26.860
I don't buy the Truffaut thing, either...

00:14:26.860 --> 00:14:30.100
Didn't Truffaut make romances for adults?

00:14:30.100 --> 00:14:35.240
You need to understand the subtleties 
of relationships to get them.

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:40.550
At fifteen, a girl with lots of relationship 
experience wouldn't watch Truffaut.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.270
O-Oh...

00:14:42.280 --> 00:14:43.720
Right?

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:45.910
Now, a question...

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:49.670
Russian literature, with its 
rich human dramas.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:52.690
Truffaut, with his depictions 
of adult romance.

00:14:52.690 --> 00:14:55.310
Both are highly regarded and artistic.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:58.710
And if you say you like them, 
you seem very smart...

00:14:59.110 --> 00:15:01.880
At least, to other people.

00:15:01.880 --> 00:15:03.020
I get it.

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:06.560
So she chose them to seem smart, right?

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:08.710
And not because she likes them.

00:15:09.060 --> 00:15:12.550
No, maybe she thinks she does like them.

00:15:13.330 --> 00:15:18.930
It's hard to think she truly understands 
Truffaut or Russian literature.

00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:21.460
But I don't see her as a simple liar.

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:25.810
So maybe she's just gilding herself.

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:27.240
Gilding?

00:15:27.470 --> 00:15:30.580
Maybe Konatsu-chan has a problem.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:33.170
Be careful how you deal with her.

00:15:33.160 --> 00:15:34.410
Hmm...

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:35.920
And her, too.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:39.830
She ain't watching Truffaut...

00:15:41.560 --> 00:15:42.820
Hey, there!

00:15:44.170 --> 00:15:45.290
<b>Gull</b>

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:49.950
She insulted our club, 
but she's the first here.

00:15:49.950 --> 00:15:50.960
Hey, now...

00:15:50.960 --> 00:15:51.910
Hello!

00:15:51.910 --> 00:15:53.470
Senpai?

00:15:53.470 --> 00:15:56.630
Look at Inaba's lunch for 
today! It's amazing!

00:15:56.630 --> 00:15:58.510
It's so pretty!

00:15:58.510 --> 00:16:01.830
The yellow things are shrimp dumplings 
with a corn coating,

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:04.220
and the colorful ones are 
chop suey spring rolls.

00:16:04.220 --> 00:16:06.320
And the rose is salmon!

00:16:06.320 --> 00:16:08.230
I'm so jealous!

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:11.150
Konatsu-chan, want to see Inaba's lunch, too?

00:16:12.010 --> 00:16:13.570
I'm not interested!

00:16:15.250 --> 00:16:16.330
Oh...

00:16:16.730 --> 00:16:18.690
Also, Tashiro-senpai.

00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:22.540
Please don't call me by my first name.

00:16:22.540 --> 00:16:25.570
I have a last name. Yamamoto.

00:16:25.970 --> 00:16:27.470
I... I see.

00:16:27.470 --> 00:16:29.650
I'm sorry, Yamamoto-san.

00:16:32.570 --> 00:16:36.590
Hey, there! I rented
DVDs for the anime choices!

00:16:37.460 --> 00:16:38.730
Thanks.

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:42.350
Senpai, it took three places, 
but I finally got them all.

00:16:42.600 --> 00:16:44.120
Which do you want?

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.490
There are so many, it's hard to choose.

00:16:46.490 --> 00:16:50.120
They all look great... My tension's rising!

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:52.860
That isn't how you use the word "tension."

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:54.660
What?

00:16:54.660 --> 00:16:58.350
I said that isn't how you 
use the word "tension."

00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:02.030
In English, "tension" is used 
to refer to a nervous state.

00:17:02.220 --> 00:17:03.820
I didn't know that.

00:17:03.820 --> 00:17:08.010
Y-Yeah, that's true. But that's 
how we use it in Japanese.

00:17:08.010 --> 00:17:09.180
So it's okay, right?

00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:13.750
You're in the English Conversation Club, 
and you didn't even know that?

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.820
Hey, you didn't need to put it that way.

00:17:18.820 --> 00:17:20.810
As long as people understand, who cares?

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:24.410
You're using English wrong, despite being 
in the English Conversation Club?

00:17:24.410 --> 00:17:26.800
Why not take a little more pride?

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.080
We're speaking Japanese, 
and that's how we use it.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.940
We don't think about it that much!

00:17:33.160 --> 00:17:35.940
"We"? Is that the royal we?

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:38.920
Please don't say things to 
detract from your responsibility.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.860
The royal... what was it?

00:17:43.410 --> 00:17:46.670
The royal we exists to make an 
individual's feelings appear

00:17:46.670 --> 00:17:48.460
to be those of a group.

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:50.440
It's the "we" of a ruler.

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:53.990
The name comes from its use by 
royalty when speaking to subjects.

00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:58.290
So a commoner shouldn't use it.

00:17:58.740 --> 00:18:01.100
H-Huh? Then, what?

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:03.420
If I'm a commoner pretending to be king,

00:18:03.420 --> 00:18:05.060
then what are you?

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:11.240
I don't use English improperly 
or deflect responsibility.

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:15.690
So... So...

00:18:15.690 --> 00:18:20.110
So you're talking much more like a king!

00:18:20.420 --> 00:18:21.420
Hey.

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:24.350
Stop being stupid and get ready.

00:18:24.350 --> 00:18:25.670
The club president is coming.

00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:27.790
But...

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:29.900
What do you mean by "stupid"?

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:33.340
How am I stupid?

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:35.360
I didn't mean you.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:36.800
Enough, Yamamoto.

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:37.300
<b>Gull</b>

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:40.460
You're going to ignore me?!

00:18:45.530 --> 00:18:46.710
Yamamoto?

00:18:55.580 --> 00:18:57.610
What was that? I don't believe it!

00:18:57.610 --> 00:18:59.990
Jeez!

00:18:59.990 --> 00:19:01.980
<i>I just don't get it!</i>

00:19:01.980 --> 00:19:03.930
<i>How arrogant can you be?</i>

00:19:03.930 --> 00:19:06.660
<i>She doesn't listen, and I don't 
know what she's saying!</i>

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:09.490
<i>I can't take this, damn it!</i>

00:19:11.010 --> 00:19:12.590
She sounds cute.

00:19:12.590 --> 00:19:19.680
You only say that because you're sure 
that you're far smarter than she is.

00:19:19.680 --> 00:19:20.870
<i>Of course.</i>

00:19:20.870 --> 00:19:21.920
Damn it!

00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:26.840
But you didn't say, "That's why you 
can't make friends," did you?

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:29.340
<i>No, not yet.</i>

00:19:29.340 --> 00:19:30.510
There, there...

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:34.560
<i>You think there's some 
problem with her, right?</i>

00:19:35.340 --> 00:19:36.770
Well, yeah.

00:19:37.140 --> 00:19:40.310
<i>This is another new meeting, huh?</i>

00:19:40.820 --> 00:19:43.130
<i>Jeez, I've had enough of them.</i>

00:19:43.130 --> 00:19:45.420
When I was a kid?

00:19:45.690 --> 00:19:48.510
Well, I had plenty of money.

00:19:48.510 --> 00:19:52.220
So I spent middle school through 
university playing with it.

00:19:52.220 --> 00:19:54.420
But I suppose I studied, too.

00:19:55.080 --> 00:19:56.960
I met a lot of people.

00:19:56.960 --> 00:19:59.600
Fun people and crazy people.

00:20:00.450 --> 00:20:02.860
Some of them were always no good.

00:20:02.860 --> 00:20:05.980
But some reformed and contributed to society.

00:20:06.210 --> 00:20:11.270
But whether they could reform 
or not was their problem.

00:20:11.690 --> 00:20:14.710
And when that happens, nobody is focused on what's going on around them.

00:20:14.710 --> 00:20:17.880
Whom you can see and when

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:22.840
all may be fated, from the start.

00:20:23.820 --> 00:20:26.540
<i>Your fate... huh?</i>

00:20:27.150 --> 00:20:30.590
<i>Does Yamamoto have a fate like that?</i>

00:20:34.530 --> 00:20:36.300
"People are changing.

00:20:36.300 --> 00:20:38.450
They are becoming like us."

00:20:38.450 --> 00:20:40.370
So cute!

00:20:40.370 --> 00:20:41.850
Hey, there!

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:45.220
Yamamoto's absent again today, huh?

00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:48.480
She could say something...

00:20:48.830 --> 00:20:50.470
If she's going to be absent often,

00:20:50.470 --> 00:20:53.290
wouldn't Sakaguchi-sensei, 
our adviser, say something?

00:20:53.800 --> 00:20:56.400
For now, I'll just have to watch.

00:20:56.750 --> 00:21:01.600
<i>True, there may be nothing we can do now.</i>

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:06.820
It's time to turn to the Petits, master!

00:21:08.060 --> 00:21:09.060
No, thanks.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:10.990
Hey, master...

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:13.810
Inaba! Help me with this!

00:21:13.810 --> 00:21:14.760
Sure.

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:17.830
It's raining!

00:21:33.740 --> 00:21:38.050
<i>And so, my chaotic second semester began.</i>

00:23:11.240 --> 00:23:13.520
Isn't the moon mysterious?

00:23:13.520 --> 00:23:15.950
When I look at it, I remember the past,

00:23:15.950 --> 00:23:17.750
and my heart skips a beat!

00:23:17.750 --> 00:23:19.580
Sounds kind of romantic...

00:23:19.580 --> 00:23:21.800
And I feel like howling, too.

00:23:23.600 --> 00:23:26.420
M-Mariko-san, you're a ghost, right?

00:23:27.070 --> 00:23:30.010
Next time on <i>Elegant Yokai Apartment Life</i>:

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:32.230
"Look at the Full Moon and Jump."

00:23:30.010 --> 00:23:32.510
<b>Sixteenth Haunting 
Look at the Full Moon and Jump</b>

00:23:32.780 --> 00:23:36.470
I wonder if Heaven is above the sky after all.
